## [ENT-093] | 2026-11-17 17:05 UTC | Unity | error | ref: scripts/intel-index.py | see: queue.log ENT-170
Class: a gate run on one file that cannot see what only the whole set shows (the family of a rule nothing checks: ENT-084, ENT-087, ENT-088, ENT-089).
Case: on 2026-11-17 at 16:39:40 UTC my hourly tracker gave game/planets/n-maia.md the id 20261117T163940Z (one of 50 files of that pass, commit 5a8a067 at 16:41 UTC). In the same second Military took its `date -u` for the report reports/2026-11-17_apophis_escort-follow-built-far-bids-gone-curd-stored.md. The report's gate, as my skill report-admiral wrote it, ran `validate-ids.sh` on the one file, which compares only the files it is given, read PASS, and the report was committed at 16:43 UTC.
Effect: from 16:43 to 16:57 UTC `bash scripts/validate-ids.sh` on the whole repository read `DUPLICATE ID`, and every install (install_when_clean.sh, fleet-build.sh) and the tracker's own gate would have halted. One install of mine halted at 16:53 UTC; I know of no other (Military's turn ended at 16:45 UTC, the next turn is mine). No data lost.
Cause, mine twice: (1) new_id() of intel-index.py read only the ids of the two intel folders and counted forward from now, into seconds that had not been yet, 50 in a row; (2) the report skills told every member to run the id gate on the report alone.
Fix, done: n-maia.md has a new id (commit 37b8957; the report is untouched); new_id() takes the first free second going back from now against every Markdown file of the repository (ids_in_use; test test_a_new_id_is_free_in_the_whole_repository_and_never_a_second_to_come; commit c09d0b8; on the old code the test fails at its first call, which cannot be given a time); the skills report-admiral, report-unity and session-end run `bash scripts/validate-ids.sh` without a file name and say what a DUPLICATE ID line asks of the member.
Would it have prevented this one: yes, at the report: the whole-repository gate names the report at 16:43 UTC, before its commit, and its member takes a new id. The tracker cannot see a member's draft outside the clone, so the gate at the commit is the half that holds.
Still open, asked of Morpheus in queue.log: validate-ids.sh given file names compares them with each other only; a member's hand that runs it so still reads PASS on a duplicate.

## [ENT-094] | 2026-11-17 18:38 UTC | Unity | error | ref: game/fleet/hive.py | see: reports.log ENT-074
Class: a figure that misled: a money window told as the true one while the event that bent the hour lay inside it too.
Case: my turn's report of 18:28 UTC (reports.log ENT-074) and its summary to Suggi told the fleet's steady money as -27,458 cr an hour over 6 hours and -18,155 over 24 hours, read at 18:06 UTC, and called the 6-hour figure the honest one beside a last hour of -148,544 cr bent by my sweep into the treasury. The sweep's gifts (189,040 cr booked before the receiving wallet showed them) lay inside the longer windows as well: about 31,500 cr an hour of the 6-hour figure and about 7,900 of the 24-hour one. Read again at 18:33 UTC, the receivers' wallets read: -877 cr an hour over 6 hours, -11,178 over 24 hours.
Effect: Suggi was told a steady loss about 26,000 cr an hour larger than it was. What rests on it holds: the fleet's steady money is still at or below zero, and the no to the station core rests on the total and the 24-hour figure. Corrected to him in my chat at 19:45 CET. The report file is left as written; this entry corrects it.
Cause: `hive.py fleet` takes a giver's wallet at once and a receiver's when the fleet file next reads it; a window that ends between the two counts the gift as money gone. I knew it for the hour (my knowledge file on money figures) and did not see that a longer window holds the same sum, divided by its hours.
Fix, done: the corrected figures told; the skill report-unity now says that every window containing such an event is bent by the event's sum over its hours, and that the figure is told with that sum taken out or read again once the receivers' wallets were read. The same skill now names two lines the summary left out this turn: the Voidborn Mastery levels by role (rule F35) and every item of the turn's open build list as built or not built.
Fix, to build in my turn of 21:30 UTC with the sweep script (DECISIONS Q69 (1)): `hive.py fleet` holds a gift whose receiver's wallet was not read after it out of every window and prints the sum held out; the test: a gift booked, the receiver's reading older than the gift, the three nets unchanged.
Would it have prevented this one: the skill line, yes for the telling (the 6-hour figure would have been told as about +4,000 or read again); the script, yes for the figure itself.

